app orb-serve-check-spec [
  version: "1.0.0",
  description: "Design contract for `orb serve-check PROGRAM [--port N] [--cwd DIR]` (replaces the native half of tools/orb-serve-e2e/run.sh with the same commands). The orb binary is $ORB_BIN (default orb on the PATH). WORKING DIRECTORY: --cwd, default <invocation directory>/packages/almadar-std (run.sh ran in packages/almadar-std). PORT: --port, default a free port the OS hands out, asked of python3 (`import socket; s=socket.socket(); s.bind((127.0.0.1,0)); print(s.getsockname()[1])`) as run.sh did. START: a shell runs, in the working directory, `ORB_NO_AUTO_SETUP=1 DATA_BACKEND=mock NODE_ENV=development $ORB_BIN serve PROGRAM --port PORT --no-mock --no-emulators` in the background with stdout and stderr in <mktemp -d>/serve.log and answers `<pid> <tempdir>`. READY: `curl -sf http://127.0.0.1:PORT/api/health` once a second until it exits 0, at most 120 tries; no answer is `FAIL  orb serve did not answer /api/health`. OUTPUT, in order: `--- who listens on :PORT` and the unique `<command> <pid>` pairs of `lsof -nP -iTCP:PORT -sTCP:LISTEN`; `FAIL  the listener is not orb` when no pair is orb; `--- node/bun processes on this machine (the runner below is the only one allowed to be new)` then the `ps -axo pid,command` lines naming node or bun and the port, the temp directory or serve.log, or `none serving :PORT`; then one line per check, `PASS  <name>` or `FAIL  <name>`: `the page is served by orb serve` (GET / answers 200 with a body), `the wasm kernel is served by orb serve` (the .wasm named by the entry script of GET / answers 200 with content-type application/wasm), `a stream ticket is minted` (POST /api/events/ticket answers 200 with a ticket), `a spent ticket is refused` (the ticket is used once on GET /api/events?clientId=spend&ticket=T with curl -m 2, then again with clientId=replay: the second answer is 401). On any FAIL the serve.log is printed after the lines. The server is killed and the temp directory removed in every case. Status 200 (exit 0) when every line is PASS, 500 (exit 1) otherwise. A missing PROGRAM, an unknown flag or a further word is a usage error (status 400, exit 2). The checks that need a page (the rows render, the live stream opens in a page with a ticket, no token in any URL, a search dispatches an event, the /api/orbitals/register note) stay in tools/orb-serve-e2e/e2e.mjs until the browser operators observe a page's requests (G-ORB-446)."
]

orbital OrbServeCheckSpec {
  expects trait OrbServeCheck {
    state ready
    state parsing
    state starting
    state polling
    state checking
    state finishing
    emits {
      SERVE_CHECK_ANSWERED { status : number!  body : string! }
    }
  }
  expects page boot -> OrbServeCheck
}
